{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/984612-miss-peregrine\u2019s-home-for-peculiar-children-in-cofd","id":984612,"title":"Miss Peregrine\u2019s Home For Peculiar Children in CofD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-09T15:11:37-07:00","id":984612,"title":"Miss Peregrine\u2019s Home For Peculiar Children in CofD","content":"It\u2019s interesting movie \u2013 a bit light hearted to most <b>CoD</b> interpretations, but there is darker edge to it. When I saw first trailers I thought It will be <b>Changeling</b> story about misfits running from life. It surely has this tone, but to me it much better works as <b>Mage</b> 2E story, where Miss Peregrine is Acanthus governing \u2018school\u2019 of Sleepwalkers with odd talents. ( Remember: In <b>Mage</b> any person with innate powers is treated as Sleepwalker. ) There are time travel shenanigans and some transhumanist overtones later in movie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DN1uhnnKscY\" data-code=\"DN1uhnnKscY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/DN1uhnnKscY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-09-2016, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T15:17:15-07:00","id":984615,"title":"","content":"... Just seen it. <br /> <br /> Lots of Changeling fuel there.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think though it might work best as a &quot;Home&quot; for &quot;everyone&quot;. Every splat, template, and minor template. Remember, the setting is implied to be big, featuring other places as well. Ergo, there's some places with more representation for a given splat, others would not have X splat, and so forth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T11:55:05-07:00","id":984980,"title":"","content":"Saw it the other night. In terms of setting it's Mage, imo. But thematically it felt very much more Beast. I don't want to give detailed reasons though because of Spoilers. What I will say though, is I knew next to nothing about it when I went in and as I watched the stars names go by... Judi Dench, Terrence Stamp, Samuel L. Jackson and others, I got more and more interested. I didn't recognize the lead's name but when I saw him I immediately went &quot;Oh, Ender's Game! Fantastic!&quot;. I don't think anybody put a foot wrong in that film - even the younger children were really good.<br /> <br /> Samuel L. Jackson was *really* enjoying himself in that film. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T12:41:40-07:00","id":985004,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11763_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11763\" data-vbnamecard=\"11763\">knasser</a> , I see you agree on <b>Mage</b> points. I could see some low-level <b>Changeling</b> here. But then you made me intrigued on <b>Beast</b> reading. If you do not want to spoil people, maybe make your arguments in [SPOILER] tag? Because I'm really interested in this take on movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T05:35:57-07:00","id":985362,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. Well...<br /> <br /> At the most superficial level, the home reminded me a lot of a Beast's lair - out of the ordinary world and an inaccessible refuge and all the children kind of pool them together. There's the little girl's garden, there's the boy's horrifying doll collosseum-cum-surgery. It's just the sense of community and isolation of it.<br /> <br /> But on a more meaningful level, I don't think it works as Mage in terms of characters. Yes, the world is large and contains mysteries, but the children aren't exploring those mysteries, they don't acquire abilities through learning or insight, rather their ability (singular except in the case of Miss Peregrine and kind-of in the case of Emma) is a mark upon them or part of who they are. A mage to me is someone who does multiple things, changes the world around them and in some sense their abilities develop as extensions of themselves. The children's abilities feel much more like gifts than a product of who they are. I mean admittedly the fire girl has red-hair, but women with fire powers always have red-hair. None of it felt like it was about perception or insight. Additionally I see mages as withdrawing from the world. They're the old man in the tower or the woman in the woods. (and before anyone questions my adoption of gender norms, towers are phallic and woods are dark and moist so don't blame me for mythic archetypes!). Whereas the children are more like Beast from Le Belle et la Bette - driven out or excluded from society. Sure, there's overlap, but this is what I grab at first for comparisons.<br /> <br /> Plus, I feel a Mage story would have more emphasis on the unknown, more sense of mystery in its plot and setting. This film had monsters. People who had turned into monsters. (I don't think it's a spoiler to say that). And a film with monsters, especially when those monsters - well, they seem a lot like <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">people who have merged with their beasts, giving up their humanity.</div></div> </div> </div>.<br /> <br /> Also, maybe if nothing else, Eva Green feels way more like a Beast than a Mage. She has this way of growling when she talks and my, what big eyes she has! All the way through that movie, you get the feeling she might be about to devour someone. Did you catch the blink-and-you'll-miss-it way she ate in the dinner scene? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":11763,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","user":"knasser","date":". 10-11-2016, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T06:43:24-07:00","id":985384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/984612-miss-peregrine\u2019s-home-for-peculiar-children-in-cofd?p=985362#post985362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But on a more meaningful level, I don't think it works as Mage in terms of characters. Yes, the world is large and contains mysteries, but the children aren't exploring those mysteries, they don't acquire abilities through learning or insight, rather their ability (singular except in the case of Miss Peregrine and kind-of in the case of Emma) is a mark upon them or part of who they are. A mage to me is someone who does multiple things, changes the world around them and in some sense their abilities develop as extensions of themselves. The children's abilities feel much more like gifts than a product of who they are. I mean admittedly the fire girl has red-hair, but women with fire powers always have red-hair. None of it felt like it was about perception or insight. Additionally I see mages as withdrawing from the world. They're the old man in the tower or the woman in the woods. (and before anyone questions my adoption of gender norms, towers are phallic and woods are dark and moist so don't blame me for mythic archetypes!). Whereas the children are more like Beast from Le Belle et la Bette - driven out or excluded from society. Sure, there's overlap, but this is what I grab at first for comparisons.</div> </div> </div> </div>You see, here is the way you do not understand my argument - this was <b>Mage</b> <i>setting</i> story, not Awakened story per se. The only possible witch in all the story is Miss Peregrine ( i.e. Eva Green ) - she manipulates Time ( on Masters level I must add ) and is shapechanging, being and <i>feeling</i> as 'bigger character' than any other Peculiar. All other Peculiars are just 'Weird Talents' - also known as psychics, gifted, you know - Lesser Templates. They are not even Proximi in there as there are no 'witches' beside Miss Peregrine.<br /> <br /> Whole center on this theory is that in <b>Mage</b> 2E, Awakened take care of Lesser Templates people, even inducting them in to their Orders at lower levels. Just see Appendix One: Supporting Cast of <b>Mage</b> 2E corebook - all the psychics, all the mediums and thaumaturges are now part of protection from mages. Hell, even Wolf-Blooded, Fae-Touched or Ghouls can be seen as falling under this take, but I would still see them more as appropriate gamelines Template first. Still, mages 'take care' of everyone with supernatural powers, guys from <b>Second Sight</b> book on first opportunity.<br /> <br /> And children from Home are great examples of those kind of 'wierd people'. To add even more tie-ins to <b>Mage </b>setting, we have at least one soon-to-be-Necromances/Alchemist child and all others with more or less 'unusual' powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/984612-miss-peregrine\u2019s-home-for-peculiar-children-in-cofd?p=985362#post985362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Eva Green feels way more like a Beast than a Mage. She has this way of growling when she talks and my, what big eyes she has! All the way through that movie, you get the feeling she might be about to devour someone. Did you catch the blink-and-you'll-miss-it way she ate in the dinner scene? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Problem as Beast!Peregrine than Mage!Peregrine is that headmistress do not seem in any way 'scary'. She doesn't seem to have Horror in her soul. She just have weird powers over Time and like to be a bird from time to time. And the glow in the eyes can easily be just Nimbus effect of her - Nimbus slips also when under stress or Virtue or Vice related situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-11-2016, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:13:29-07:00","id":985523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/984612-miss-peregrine\u2019s-home-for-peculiar-children-in-cofd?p=985384#post985384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You see, here is the way you do not understand my argument - this was <b>Mage</b> <i>setting</i> story, not Awakened story per se.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't realised you were putting forth an argument. You said you were interested in my take. But in so far as I did disagree with what you said in that I said I didn't think it was Mage, I did state that I didn't feel that it works as Mage &quot;in terms of characters&quot;. The thing with the setting of Mage is that it can easily encompass the setting of Perculiar Children and still have room for a dozen other settings, too. So certainly you could draw on this film for Mage. But in so far as the Mage setting has to include mages to really be the Mage setting, I didn't feel such characters were present for the reasons given.<br /> <br /> For me, the film resonated more as a Beast story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/984612-miss-peregrine\u2019s-home-for-peculiar-children-in-cofd?p=985384#post985384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem as Beast!Peregrine than Mage!Peregrine is that headmistress do not seem in any way 'scary'. She doesn't seem to have Horror in her soul.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">She killed the landlord of the pub. Twice! And the character is pretty scary, imo, the way she moves, the way she eats. I'm tempted to say maybe it's just a little subtle.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm not interested in debating which view is most accurate. Sorry.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:39:36-07:00","id":985729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, maybe if nothing else, Eva Green feels way more like a Beast than a Mage. She has this way of growling when she talks and my, what big eyes she has! All the way through that movie, you get the feeling she might be about to devour someone. Did you catch the blink-and-you'll-miss-it way she ate in the dinner scene? </div> </div> </div>Well, she played as Morgan in the Camelot serie. I guess she picked a few..habits <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T22:37:37-07:00","id":985954,"title":"","content":"Eve also played Vanessa Ives in Penny Dreadful - also sometimes disturbing and 'witchy' role. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}